    "summary": "The square sticky-rice cakes of Bo Dau village, wrapped in wild dong leaves and boiled in village well water, chewy, fragrant and beautifully formed.",
    "story": "Bo Dau village, on the highway through Thai Nguyen, is famous for making banh chung year-round. The secret lies in fragrant upland sticky rice, lush wild dong leaves, and the crystal-clear village well water used for boiling. Bo Dau banh chung is a beloved local gift that travelers love to pick up when passing through.",
