    "summary": "Fresh fish from Thac Ba Lake clamped in bamboo and grilled over charcoal, seasoned with mac khen and doi seeds, its skin golden and fragrant with the flavors of Yen Bai's waters.",
    "story": "Thac Ba Lake, dotted with over a thousand islands, is a bounty of sweet freshwater fish for Yen Bai. Fishermen clamp their fresh-caught fish between bamboo sticks, season them with mac khen and doi seeds, and grill them over glowing charcoal by the shore. This aromatic grilled fish is an unforgettable experience for visitors exploring the vast lake.",
