    "story": "Banh xiu pao followed Chinese settlers to Nam Dinh and became a snack woven into the memories of generations of Thanh Nam schoolchildren. The dough is rolled thin in many layers and baked crisp and flaky, enclosing a filling of five-spice char siu pork and salted egg yolk. This dainty, golden little pastry is at its best while still warm.",
