    "story": "In the seaside districts of Thái Thụy and Diêm Điền in Thái Bình, gỏi nhệch is an elaborate dish reserved for honored guests. The slippery spiny eel is cleaned of its slime, thinly sliced and tossed with toasted rice powder and seasonings until 'cooked' by the acidity. The magic lies in the thick, golden chẻo sauce simmered from the fish bones with galangal and fermented rice, wrapped with an array of wild leaves into an unforgettable layering of flavor.",
